{"id":"austurbane","title":"Austurbane","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Austurbane","rev":239184,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Austurbane"]}," is a style aesthetic and product photography design that emerged in the late 2010s, coined as a term derived from \"austere\" and \"urbane,\" it diffuses stark minimalism with earthy, upscale sophistication."]},{"t":"p","c":["The typography is often characterized by a sleek, pared-down, sterile, modern version of ",{"t":"a","c":["Frasurbane"],"id":"frasurbane"},", replacing cluttered intellectual nostalgia with zen-like, clean minimalism."]}],"sections":[{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["The typography relies on editorial, elegant, serif fonts utilized alongside vast amounts of whitespace, with shadows and lightning that features dramatic, sharper lighting often casting branch shadows and realistic plants across the frame."]},{"t":"p","c":["Refractive or prismatic elements are frequently utilized to subtly scatter light, with a color palette that frequently relies on neutral, muted earth tones incorporating black, copper, beige, cream and bronze. Product photography compositions would have a curated, highly staged feel, often using geometric isometric angles or strict top-down (flat lay) along with the materials emphasizing high-quality natural, raw materials such as marble, textured granite, rough stone, structured fabrics and organic ceramics."]}]},{"title":"Media","id":"media","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Brands"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Æcorn Aperitifs"]},{"c":["Marco"]},{"c":["Rare by Nature"]},{"c":["The Row"]},{"c":["Prada"]},{"c":["Miu Miu"]},{"c":["Prada"]},{"c":["Claudiana Beautanica"]}]}]},{"title":"Gallery","id":"gallery","blocks":[{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/68/Original_a8e6d70328bf8d3fbf72e741890bf968.png/revision/latest?cb=20260605042504","w":185,"h":185},{"src":"https://static.wikia.n